Sure! Below is a simple example of an “interactive card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the card on the page */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* Card container */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Needed for 3D effect */
}

/* Card inner wrapper – this is what actually rotates */
.card-inner {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform .6s ease-in-out;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;   /* Keep children in 3D space */
}

/* Hover effect – rotate around Y‑axis */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-front h2 {
    font-size:1.5rem;
    margin-bottom:.5rem;
}
.card-front p {
    color:#555;
}

/* Back face styling */
.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);   /* Position back side opposite front */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back h3 {
    font-size:1.4rem;
    margin-bottom:.5rem;
}
.card-back p {
    color:#333;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <h2>Front Title</h2>
            <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <h3>Back Title</h3>
            <p>This is the back side of the card.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card` | Sets the size and adds `perspective` so the rotation looks 3‑dimensional. |
| `.card-inner` | Holds both faces and is the element that gets rotated. |
| `.card-face` | Base style for each face (positioned absolutely, same size). |
| `.card-front` | Front side – normal orientation. |
| `.card-back` | Back side – rotated 180° on Y‑axis so it starts hidden. |
| `backface-visibility:hidden` | Hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transition:transform .6s ease-in-out` | Smooth animation. |

When you hover over the `.card`, the `.card-inner` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face.  
Feel free to replace the content, colors, or dimensions to fit your design. Enjoy!
